\newlabel{fig:convergence}{{7}{9}{\textbf {Val-VQA training curves across phases.} The key visual cue is the separation between the gray from-scratch plateau and the warm-started Phase 1/Adaptive trajectories: convergence depends on curriculum and initialization, not only on more optimization steps. Phase 1 v3 (hard drop, LoRA r=32, blue) converges monotonically to 0.3334 at 50K steps. Phase 1 Final (token merge, r=64, red square) reaches 0.3342 at 80K despite added merge complexity. Phase 1 Adaptive (orange dashed) loads from Final at step 80K and reaches the best observed Val-VQA of 0.2879 at step 100K (20K adaptive-budget steps), then begins regressing — consistent with the upper edge of the stable $\lambda _b$ window characterized in Section~\ref {sec:budget-collapse}. Gray band: three from-scratch attempts plateaued at 0.43--0.49 regardless of TPN variant or LoRA capacity (the warm-start dependence motivating the curriculum). Downstream benchmarks do not track Val-VQA monotonically; see Table~\ref {tab:main}}{figure.7}{}}
\newlabel{sec:comparison}{{5.5}{9}{}{subsection.5.5}{}}
\newlabel{tab:main}{{6}{10}{Main results on LLaVA-1.5-7B. Cells \texttt {[E1]} are populated by the LoRA-576 control eval; \texttt {[E2]} by merge-disabled; \texttt {[E5]}/\texttt {[E6]} by MMBench/MME/TextVQA evals (run on the existing Phase 1 Final checkpoint). Published numbers are from the cited papers. \textbf {Note:} the headline comparison is TC-ViTok Final \emph {vs.\ LoRA-576}, not vs.\ published LLaVA-1.5. All TC-ViTok rows are single-seed evaluations; approximate binomial standard errors at the listed sample sizes are $\sigma \!\approx \!0.16$ pp for VQAv2 test-dev, $\approx \!0.22$ pp for GQA, and $\approx \!0.50$ pp for the 5K POPE subset}{table.6}{}}
\newlabel{tab:seed-replication}{{7}{10}{\textbf {Two-seed replication of the matched LoRA-576 gap.} Both rows are 5K-sample evaluations after 80K-step Phase 1 training with identical configuration and different seeds. The compression gap persists on seed 7}{table.7}{}}
\newlabel{fig:bars}{{8}{10}{Benchmark comparison. TC-ViTok Final (red) and Adaptive (orange) both exceed full LLaVA-1.5 on GQA (61.0\%) using only 25\% of tokens. The LoRA-576 control (70.55\% GQA, 86.46\% POPE) is the compression-isolated reference: Final is $-3.4$ GQA and $-7.4$ POPE below it, an honest $4{\times }$ selected-token compression cost. v3 GQA and POPE are now measured from checkpoint (E10): 59.87\% / 78.50\%}{figure.8}{}}
