\newlabel{fig:budget-hist}{{9}{11}{\textbf {Per-sample token-budget distribution learned by the BudgetPredictor on GQA val\_balanced.} Histogram of $k_{\mathrm {eff}}$ values assigned by the BudgetPredictor at $\lambda _b{=}0.1$. The mode is far above the fixed $k{=}144$ used by TC-ViTok Final, indicating that at this $\lambda _b$ value the predictor sees little incentive to compress aggressively. A larger $\lambda _b$ would shift the mode left; the full sweep is left for future work (Section~\ref {sec:limits})}{figure.9}{}}
\newlabel{tab:pareto}{{8}{11}{Adaptive budget operating points. $k_{\mathrm {eff}}$ is the mean soft token count; hard selection is capped at $k_{\max }{=}288$. Only $\lambda _b{=}0.10$ was measured; we report it as a single design exploration rather than a Pareto sweep (see Section~\ref {sec:limits})}{table.8}{}}
